# Code owners — who must approve changes to each path.
#
# With "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in the branch protection for
# main (and "Required approvals" set to 0), a PR needs an approval from the
# owner of every path it touches — and no approval at all for paths that have
# no owner.
#
# Everything is owned by the maintainers team, except tutorials.data.yaml,
# which is deliberately left unowned. That file is pure content data (tag labels and
# the tutorial list), strictly validated by scripts/data-schema.js in the
# required "Check build" status, so a PR touching only that file can be merged
# by its author as soon as CI is green. A PR touching anything else — code,
# workflows, this file, deploy/ — needs a review from a team member. The team
# must have Write access to the repository for GitHub to honour it here.
#
# No bot account or token is involved: the carve-out is entirely this file
# plus the branch protection settings (see README.md → "Content data").

# Default: everything requires a maintainers-team review.
*                       @uppsala-makerspace/maintainers

# Content data: unowned on purpose. A later pattern with no owner overrides
# the default above for this path.
/tutorials.data.yaml
